{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779736558,"nonce":"mPSC2OmZGw5hPX+gpGK57RPhRFg=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDmdi5g","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/164#issuecomment-4536623846"},"message":"Possible lead for the asymmetry from the #124 §2 turning analysis ([PR #172](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/172), `docs/analysis/dynamics/turning.py`): the **zero-yaw steering center sits at ~1435 PWM, not 1500** — a ~65 µs trim offset, consistent across 05-01/21/22. A steering zero that isn't centered means equal left/right rudder *commands* produce unequal thrust-vector angles, which could plausibly bias one heading direction. Worth checking whether that offset (and any port/stbd thrust-vector asymmetry) lines up with the SE-bound-only undulation, vs. a pure controller/PID-direction effect. Just a lead, not a confirmed cause.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779745127,"nonce":"ylSm7HNZo8Kkw2RMRzrE+rPUMCc=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDnOM6w","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/164#issuecomment-4537421035"},"message":"## Analysis (2026-05-22 post-mission) — undulation confirmed; SE-only asymmetry inconclusive\n\n**Undulation is real, pervasive, significant.** Per-line cross-track wobble (PCA fit to each `pattern0000/lineN` segment; 101 lines): **median 1.57 m RMS, p75 2.3 m, max ~15.9 m** on ~59 m lines. \u003e90 % of lines wobble \u003e1 m; ~37 % \u003e2 m. Confirms the field \"very undulating\" — ±2 m (worst ±16 m) leaves coverage gaps (degrades #168).\n\n**It's a tracking issue, not speed/thrust** — wobble is ~independent of speed (1.27–1.41 m/s across all wobble bins). So it's the path-follower weaving (cross-track PID limit-cycling), not low authority.\n\n**The \"SE-bound only\" asymmetry (this issue's central claim) could NOT be cleanly confirmed.** The captured line-following was predominantly **one travel heading** (~N; the survey ran ~unidirectional with transits between lines, and weaving scatters course) — so there's no clean SE/NW pair to compare within this mission. The \"straighter NW than SE\" field observation is plausible but needs a **dedicated reciprocal-line test** (clean N–S–N–S, constant speed, same conditions) to quantify.\n\n**Candidates:** CrabbingPathFollower cross-track PID over-gain → limit-cycling; interaction with the 0.5 rad/s yaw cap (corrections the clamped yaw can't execute — see #172/#124); steering bias (`ch_2` mean ~1429, below the 1500 neutral). **Fix:** follower tuning / re-enable the velocity smoother.\n\n**Recommend keeping this open**, re-scoped: undulation confirmed as a (pervasive) follower-tracking issue needing a tuning fix; the SE-only asymmetry needs a dedicated reciprocal-line test. Full write-up lands in the consolidated #169 PR.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779750306,"nonce":"sVxUO8GLhoVuh3P+hIAc5W3G8Rg=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDnoPlA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/164#issuecomment-4537847700"},"message":"**Closing — undulation characterized as far as this instance allows; reopen / re-file on recurrence *with* diagnostic data.**\n\n### What the 2026-05-22 data established (full analysis under #169)\n- **Undulation is real and significant.** Per-line cross-track wobble (PCA fit per `pattern0000/lineN`, 101 lines): **median 1.57 m RMS, p75 2.32 m, max 15.9 m** on ~59 m lines. \u003e90 % of lines wobble \u003e1 m; ~37 % \u003e2 m. Confirms the field \"very undulating\" call.\n- **It's a tracking problem, not thrust/speed.** Wobble is ~independent of boat speed (1.27–1.41 m/s across all wobble bins) — path-follower weaving, not low thrust authority.\n- **The SE-only asymmetry — this issue's central claim — could *not* be confirmed.** The captured line-following was predominantly one travel heading, so there's no clean SE/NW pair within the mission. The \"straighter NW than SE\" impression is plausible but unproven, and was likely **amplified visually by the tight ~1 m line spacing**: when wobble amplitude exceeds line spacing, the CAMP plot looks chaotic regardless of any true asymmetry (green = planned, yellow = driven).\n\n### Why we can't go further on *this* instance\nThe discriminating signal — the controller's own cross-track error and PID-term breakdown (`control_msgs/PidState`: `error`=XTE, p/i/d terms, `output`=crab command) — was **published live but not recorded**. Without it we can't separate \"validated gains limit-cycling\" from \"a disturbance/condition the gains correctly couldn't reject.\" The gains (kp ≈ −20, IzzyBoat-validated) have run clean many times, so the open question is **what was different here**, not whether to retune them.\n\n### What changes for the next run (both tracked in #173)\n1. **`pid_state` recording is now queued** — once captured, XTE + p/i/d terms + crab output settle limit-cycling vs. disturbance directly.\n2. **Yaw cap raised 0.5 → 1.0 rad/s** since this deployment ([#172](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/172) / #124 §2). A candidate mechanism here was the follower commanding yaw corrections the 0.5 rad/s clamp couldn't execute (it pinned a −2.4 rad/s request to −0.5 — see #169 §6), leaving residual cross-track error. The raised cap may itself reduce the wobble; #173 validates that on-water.\n\n### Plan\nClose now as **characterized, awaiting recurrence-with-data**. **Reopen (or file fresh) when it recurs with the `pid_state` log** — ideally via a dedicated **reciprocal-line test** (clean N–S–N–S, constant speed, same conditions) to nail the directional question. Coverage impact tracked in #168.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1779750307,"nonce":"2gWiX9Qa0tZ6sRB8FhjcV46/dGY=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDJ0COs8AAAAGCkuP9g"},"status":2}]}